  "headline": "Corn $4.64 and beans $12.47 hold; crude up 2.2% to $99.24",
  "lead": "Corn is at $4.64 overnight, up three-quarters of a cent from Wednesday's $4.63¼ settle, after lower closes. Soybeans are at $12.47, up 1¾ cents, after eight straight lower closes. Crude is the mover at $99.24, up 2.2%, as Houthi strikes on Saudi targets and Iran's ship claims lift oil.",
  "teaser": "Grains stop sliding but barely bounce, while crude climbs 2.2% to $99.24 on fresh Gulf attacks.",
