    "value": "2.69",
    "unit": "Nov soybean to Dec corn price ratio",
    "context": "Soybeans at $12.47 against corn at $4.64 gives a ratio near 2.69. That is not a low number when farmers sit down to plan next spring's acres."
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Grains stop sliding, barely",
      "body": "- Dec corn is at **$4.64** overnight, up ¾ cent, the first higher close after a streak of lower ones.\n- Soybeans are at $12.47, up 1¾ cents, and Wednesday was the eighth lower close in a row.\n- Wheat held near $6.28 as talk of Black Sea peace talks gave winter wheat some support.",
      "so_what": "Both grains moved less than two cents; the slide paused, nothing more.",
      "conviction_level": "low",
      "overnight_surprise": false
    },
    {
      "title": "Crude gains; hogs slip",
      "body": "- WTI is at **$99.24** overnight, up 2.2%, as Houthi attacks on Saudi targets and Iran's claim of seven ships hit pushed Brent above $111.\n- Lean hogs settled Wednesday at $65.73, down 2.1%, the one real loser on the livestock board.\n- Live cattle settled at $230.43, up 0.4%, and feeders at $347.83, up 0.6%.",
      "so_what": "Diesel feels the oil move first; cattle quietly held firm.",
      "conviction_level": "medium",
      "overnight_surprise": true
    }
  ],
